// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A REFUSAL NAMES ITS CAUSE. `quiet` declares `!WASI` over a body that
// reaches the host three calls down — helper, log_it, print_string, the
// library's own write — and the refusal at the declaration carries the chain
// of sites the effect enters through, read off the charge every node notes,
// down to the op of WASI it ends at. The frontier leg
// holds the chain's hops; `mentl why <this file> quiet WASI` prints the same
// chain. Until Landing 2 (2026-10-13) the message ended at `declared as
// quiet` and the developer was left to find the call by hand (measured on
// boot 6e35c6db).
import io

fn log_it(msg) = print_string(msg)

fn helper(x) = {
  log_it("x")
  x + 1
}

fn quiet(x) with !WASI = helper(x)

fn main() = quiet(1)
